Z||000000||Haze_Performance||04-10-2001||05:18 AM||||OK.. ???There is a lot more body guys in here now. I'm reintroducing an old idea I had.<P>How about cutting out the 84/86 coupe front black bumper pads and recess the opening a few inches. Then install black grills behind it? Do you know what I'm talking about? <P> <P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank><BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/haze8588logo.gif">  </A>       <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/WS6_Fiero/photo.html" TARGET=_blank><BR>Pennock's Fiero Forum Members Photo Page</A>||||reg||10
Z||000001||FieroJoe||04-10-2001||07:45 AM||||If it was metal, I bet I could do it.  Lots of experience with metal bending and welding.  As for doing something in fiberglass, I think it would just take me some time.  Also, I dont know if the fiberglass would be too ridgid for the fascia material.  I would hate to have the whole grill pop right out if the fascia flexes too much.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfixit58||04-10-2001||07:54 AM||||If I remember correctly, I believe Hot Rod Magazine or Car Craft took an 84 and removed the bumper pads and installed driving lights. I don't remember the details but I think it was an article I sent to Randy Agee ( <A HREF="http://fierozone.tripod.com/frontpage/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://fierozone.tripod.com/frontpage/index.html</A>  ) to put into his magazine section. I checked but the article isn't there.<P>Not much help but maybe some encouragement,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||2
Z||000003||jch82||04-10-2001||09:04 AM||||I think 3M makes a flexible bumper repair glue. It is 2 part and sands very easily. My uncle uses it all the time for glueing things together or repairing cracks because it allows for flex and doesn't crack (hence the name "flexible bumper repair")  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Yeah, my girlfriend takes collect calls from the road<BR>And it doesn't seem to matter that I'm lacking in the bulge<BR>She laughs at my dumb jokes when no one does<BR>She brings me mexican food from Sombrero's just because<BR>                 <I>-Blink 182</I>||||reg||1
Z||000004||flyntus||04-10-2001||09:25 AM||||Car Craft magazine did something similar in 1984/85, they cut out most of the black bumper pads, turned the turn-signal lights up vertical & in the middle & placed rectangular driving lights on the outside & fog lights on the inside. Then mounted black, opaque plexiglass to cover.  It looked great. I kept all the articles for about 7 years planning on doing my 85 but magazines got lost over the years while in the military.   Looked similar to this.<BR>              -|-          -|||208.165.3.148||reg||1
